--
inconsistent return
--
FLIPPED KNOWNBUG->CORE 2026-08-12.  Two fixes: (1) [temp.inst]/11 --
still-deferred, never odr-used members carry RAW parse trees; their
values are now cleared before goto conversion instead of leaking
un-type-checked bodies.  (2) type2name threw std::string on
`constructor`/`destructor` return types (C++ struct components include
member functions); the C++ front-end's recoveries only catch int, so
the exception escaped mid-body and left half-type-checked bodies
behind (the _Sp_counted_ptr_inplace::_M_get_deleter shape).  Now maps
them to stable CTOR/DTOR spellings ([class.ctor], [class.dtor]: no
return type -- any deterministic token).  The disallowed pattern pins
zero demotions.
